WEBVTT

00:14:29.252 --> 00:14:31.601
for a week and do satellite

00:14:31.601 --> 00:14:34.253
space experiments like that.

00:14:34.253 --> 00:14:37.009
So, as I said, there's

00:14:37.009 --> 00:14:38.568
lots of examples, and I'm going to stop here. And I just

00:14:38.568 --> 00:14:41.084
want to thank the Arduino community

00:14:41.084 --> 00:14:42.754
for being the best, and just

00:14:42.754 --> 00:14:44.946
every day making lots of projects.

00:14:44.946 --> 00:14:48.410
Thank you. (Applause)

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:50.737
(Applause)

00:14:50.737 --> 00:14:53.224
And thanks to the community.

00:14:53.224 --> 00:14:55.197
Chris Anderson: Massimo,

00:14:55.197 --> 00:14:57.802
you told me earlier today that you had no idea, of course,

00:14:57.802 --> 00:14:59.274
that it would take off like this.

00:14:59.274 --> 00:15:00.063
MB: No.